## 🌀 Bubble Sort (Basic Version)

👉 Idea:  
- Repeatedly compare **adjacent elements**.  
- If they are in the wrong order, swap them.  
- After the **1st pass**, the largest element bubbles to the end.  
- After the **2nd pass**, the second largest bubbles to its correct position, and so on.  

---

### 🔹 Code: Basic Bubble Sort
```c
#include <stdio.h>

void bubble_sort(int arr[], int n) {
    for(int i = 0; i < n-1; i++) {   // n-1 passes
        for(int j = 0; j < n-i-1; j++) {  // last i elements are already sorted
            if(arr[j] > arr[j+1]) {
                // swap arr[j] and arr[j+1]
                int temp = arr[j];
                arr[j] = arr[j+1];
                arr[j+1] = temp;
            }
        }
    }
}

int main() {
    int arr[] = {64, 34, 25, 12, 22, 11, 90};
    int n = sizeof(arr)/sizeof(arr[0]);

    printf("Original array: ");
    for(int i=0; i<n; i++) printf("%d ", arr[i]);
    printf("\n");

    bubble_sort(arr, n);

    printf("Sorted array: ");
    for(int i=0; i<n; i++) printf("%d ", arr[i]);
    printf("\n");

    return 0;
}
```

